cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LINCHPIN, please cite the software as below."
title: "LINCHPIN: read-only attack-path reasoning and minimum-cut remediation planning"
abstract: >-
  LINCHPIN fuses already-collected scanner (OpenVAS, Nessus, nmap), identity (SharpHound/BloodHound)
  and segmentation data with public exploit intelligence (NVD CVSS, FIRST EPSS, CISA KEV) into one
  attack graph, and computes the smallest set of fixes that cuts every attack path to the crown jewels
  (exact vertex min-cut with a greedy set-cover fallback), with templated, evidence-backed rationales.
type: software
authors:
